statement:
Fix a variable type $V$ and a Boolean assignment $\alpha : V \to \{\text{true}, \text{false}\}$, and consider the coloring of the reduction graph induced by $\alpha$, which sends each vertex to a color in $\{0, 1, 2\}$ (with $1$ standing for True and $2$ for False). For every literal $\ell$ over $V$, the literal node of $\ell$ receives color $1$ if $\ell$ is satisfied by $\alpha$, and color $2$ otherwise:
\[
  \text{color of the literal node of } \ell
  \;=\;
  \begin{cases} 1 & \text{if $\ell$ is satisfied by $\alpha$,}\\ 2 & \text{otherwise.}\end{cases}
\]
